## This is a sample Config file it must be located in /DD/USR/LIB/UUCP## The config file is for changing the UUCP packages defaults# used for directories, uucp's usernames, file locations and# associated filenames.## The only necessary entry is 'node', which defines your uucp# systems name and domain.## optional entries are:## uucp      Password entry for UUCP (set uid to this entry)# uuerr     Alias of the person to send errors to.# pubdir    path to UUCP Public directory (Dir where files maybe recieved)# spooldir  path to UUCP in coming/out going files# logdir    path to UUCP/UUXQT/UUCLEAN log files (relative to spooldir)# maildir   path to user mailboxes# lockdir   path to lock directory# libdir    path to lib  directory that contains the following files:#           (systems, dialers, commands, devices and perms files)# systems   systems file# dialers   dialer info# commands  legal commands for uuxqt# devices   devices info# perms     remote systems permissions (Not implemented yet)# passwd    path and name of the password file. IE: /dd/sys/passwd#           (default is /DD/SYS/Password)## node is the machines node.domain namenode      htsmm1.Las-Vegas.NV.US# spooldir uucp's spool directoryspool     /dd/spool/uucp# pubdir  where files may be transfered to ~/ or ~uucppubdir    /dd/spool/uucppublic# uucp is the user name of uucpuucp      uucp# uuerr is the local username to send error messages touuerr     uucp